  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member, I want the Tous / Favoris / Suivis / Lus filter in a sub-forum too, not only in a whole category, so that I find what I follow wherever I browse. Split from #593 (operator, 2026-11-13). Its items 3 and 4 at category level were delivered by #427 (PR #744).\n\n### What is known\n- HFR filters a sub-forum with the category list URL plus `subcat=<s>` and `owntopic=<n>`: `forum1.php?config=hfr.inc&cat=<c>&page=1&subcat=<s>&owntopic=<n>`. `R603d` (**verified**) shows that `subcat=<s>` answers 200 in place. The same 14 topics with `owntopic=1` is a run observation only (HFR-PROTOCOL §6c \"Smiley page and filtered lists\").\n- The app knows a sub-forum only by its path (`/hfr/<cat>/<sub>/liste_sujet-1.htm`). `TopicSource.supportsFlagFilter` is false for `.subforum` on purpose, and the UI says the filter applies to the whole category.\n- Where the numeric `<s>` comes from:\n  - The REST sub-category lists (#285, PR #873, `R285a`-`R285c`) give each sub-category's `id` and `name`. That `id` is the HTML `subcat` (run observation in #873).\n  - The topic rows of an HTML list carry `subcat=<s>` in their `forum2.php` links.\n  - No capture yet ties a REST `name` to a home-page sub-forum path: match on names, or read `subcat` from the rows of the sub-forum's own page.\n\n### Scope\n- Find the sub-forum's `subcat` id from captured data only. Prefer the sub-forum page's own rows; use the REST list (after #873) where no row exists. Cite which one.\n- Enable the filter on `.subforum` sources with that id; keep the shared `TopicFlagFilterPicker` and filter model of #427.\n- If no captured page gives the id for an empty sub-forum, say what to capture; never guess.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] In a sub-forum, the picker filters with `subcat=<s>&owntopic=<n>`, and the requests match the captured URL shapes.\n- [ ] Tests against committed fixtures (`R603d` and the source chosen for the id).\n- [ ] Logged out, the filter stays on Tous (as in a category).\n\n### Blocked by\nNone. #873 helps if the REST list is the chosen source.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
